        "title": "Vernacular Architecture",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Vernacular architecture is the building tradition produced by local communities\nfor local needs using local materials, without formal training. It is not primitive —\nit is multi-generational optimization under local constraints. Every regional\nvernacular tradition is essentially a solved engineering problem, refined over\ncenturies by the feedback of buildings that worked and buildings that failed."
